    "title": "Harrisburg Police investigate reported stabbing; man injured - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylee Lindenmuth ,\n2 hours ago HARRISBURG, Pa. (WHTM) -- Police are investigating a reported stabbing in Harrisburg.\nThe incident happened in the area of Rolleston and Paxton Streets late Thursday afternoon.\nPolice at the scene told abc27 News they were called for a stabbing in which a man was taken to an area hospital for treatment.\nIn a statement, Harrisburg Police said the man was conscious when police arrived.\nNumerous officers converged on the scene and taped off an area between Rolleston and Dean streets.\nOfficers said the incident appears to be isolated and there is no threat to the public.\nThe investigation remains ongoing.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC27.",
    "summary": "The incident happened in the area of Rolleston and Paxton Streets late Thursday afternoon. Police at the scene told abc27 News they were called for a stabbing in which a man was taken to an area hospital for treatment. Numerous officers converged on the scene and taped off an area between Rolleston and Dean streets. Officers said the incident appears to be isolated and there is no threat to the public. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC27.",
